B.NC={CORE:0,OPS:1,DATA:2,AI:3,TECH:4,CHANGE:5}
B.aG={formula:0,assignment:1,capstone:2,gist:3}
B.Mz=new A.b4(B.aG,["Assets = Liabilities + Equity. Profit = Revenue \u2212 Expenses. Cash differs from profit because of timing, working capital and non-cash items.","Explain one fictional month-end variance in each statement. For each, identify the source record, reconciliation and control you would test.","Prepare a one-page month-end health note with profit, financial position, cash movements, reconciliations, risks and action owners.","Performance over a period, financial position at a date and cash movement answer different questions. Tie each to evidence."],t.l)
B.MB=new A.b4(B.aG,["Working capital = Current assets \u2212 Current liabilities. CCC = DIO + DSO \u2212 DPO. Use consistent period and denominator definitions.","Build a weekly cash-risk view with opening cash, expected receipts, critical payments, confidence, owner and contingency.","Recommend a 30-day working-capital plan with baseline, segmented actions, owners, expected impact and supplier/customer risk guardrails.","Liquidity depends on timing. Improve collections, inventory and payment planning together without breaching terms."],t.l)
B.MO=new A.b4(B.aG,["Reconciliation difference = Source A \u2212 Source B. A zero difference is not enough if both sources are incomplete or share the same error.","Design a reconciliation control: purpose, sources, frequency, preparer, reviewer, tolerance, evidence, escalation and closure rules.","Create a supplier-payment control matrix listing risks, preventive/detective controls, owners, evidence and failure response.","Controls need a risk objective, owner, evidence, timely execution, independent review and a defined response to failure."],t.l)
B.KI=s([B.Mz,B.MB,B.MO],t.SN)
B.MJ=new A.b4(B.aG,["First-time match rate = invoices matched without correction \xf7 invoices processed \xd7 100%. Overdue rate = overdue unpaid invoices \xf7 total unpaid invoices \xd7 100%.","Create an exception log with supplier, invoice, amount, PO, receipt, reason, owner, age, next action, due date and escalation flag.","Propose a 30-day overdue-invoice reduction plan with root causes, weekly targets and control guardrails.","P2P speed comes from clean data, reliable matching and clear exception ownership\u2014not bypassing approvals."],t.l)
B.MP=new A.b4(B.aG,["DSO \u2248 average trade receivables \xf7 credit sales for period \xd7 days in period. Track dispute age, promise-to-pay kept rate and unapplied cash.","Prioritise five fictional overdue invoices by value, age and risk; specify action, owner, promise date and escalation.","Design an O2C sprint to reduce aged debt and unapplied cash without harming customer relationships or control quality.","Overdue is a symptom. Separate billing, delivery, credit, dispute and application issues so the right owner can resolve them."],t.l)
B.ML=new A.b4(B.aG,["Close completion = tasks completed and approved \xf7 tasks due \xd7 100%. Pair speed with post-close adjustments and aged-reconciliation metrics.","Draft a five-day close calendar with task, owner, dependency, evidence, reviewer and escalation.","Design a close dashboard tracking completion, late journals, aged reconciling items, unsupported balances and post-close corrections.","A green close status is not proof of accuracy; use cut-off, supported entries, reconciliations and review."],t.l)
B.Ks=s([B.MJ,B.MP,B.ML],t.SN)
B.MF=new A.b4(B.aG,['Example: =IF(AND([@Status]="Unpaid",[@DueDate]<$B$1),"Overdue","Not overdue"). Use SUMIFS for owner-level overdue value.',"Define a report date, overdue rule, ageing bands and duplicate key. List three tests to validate the output.","Specify an AP ageing report with formulas, KPI definitions, quality checks, owner breakdown and action list.","Define the grain and rule, clean inputs, calculate transparently, reconcile outputs and explain the action."],t.l)
B.MG=new A.b4(B.aG,["Extract \u2192 Transform \u2192 Validate \u2192 Load. Eligible source rows should equal loaded rows plus explicitly rejected/held rows after documented filters.","Document schema, type fixes, ID mapping, duplicate rules, exception handling and reconciliation checks for two monthly files.","Design a refreshable AP pipeline with source convention, mapping owner, error query, reconciliation and failure notification.","Repeatability matters only when transformations are explainable and every refresh reconciles to source."],t.l)
B.MM=new A.b4(B.aG,["Overdue rate = overdue unpaid invoice count \xf7 total unpaid invoice count \xd7 100%. Keep count-based and value-based rates distinct.","Create a KPI dictionary for overdue value, first-time match rate, blocked count and average resolution age.","Wireframe an AP dashboard with trend, breakdown, drill-through, source reconciliation and refresh/error indicators.","Reliable BI requires clear KPI definitions, correct model grain, tested measures and governed refresh."],t.l)
B.Jl=s([B.MF,B.MG,B.MM],t.SN)
B.MN=new A.b4(B.aG,["Net annual benefit = measurable annual benefit \u2212 annual run/support cost. Payback months = initial investment \xf7 monthly net benefit, if positive.","Score invoice entry, dispute resolution and monthly file consolidation for volume, rule stability, exceptions, risk and value.","Prepare an automation brief with baseline, solution choice, controls, test cases, fallback, owner and monitoring.","Automate stable work, not uncontrolled complexity; measure real benefits and include support and exception costs."],t.l)
B.MH=new A.b4(B.aG,["Field accuracy = correctly extracted and validated fields \xf7 fields tested \xd7 100%. Track false accepts separately from false rejects.","Define validation and hard-stop rules for supplier, invoice number, date, currency, tax, total and PO. Assign each exception an owner.","Design invoice processing with confidence bands, validations, human queue, audit fields, sampling and rollback.","Extraction proposes data; business validation checks it; authorised people resolve uncertainty."],t.l)
B.ME=new A.b4(B.aG,["Precision = true positive alerts \xf7 all positive alerts. Recall = true positive alerts \xf7 all actual positive cases.","Write an AI control policy covering allowed use, reviewer authority, evidence, privacy, escalation and monitoring.","Create a governance pack with risk assessment, human review workflow, test results, logs, KPIs and shutdown criteria.","AI can prioritise and assist, but accountable people verify evidence, record overrides and monitor performance."],t.l)
B.Kp=s([B.MN,B.MH,B.ME],t.SN)
B.MI=new A.b4(B.aG,["Reconciliation break = internal recorded amount \u2212 externally confirmed amount. Compare counts and IDs as well as totals.","Draw the payment lifecycle and list evidence for pending, rejected, timeout and confirmed settlement.","Specify payment reconciliation with IDs, status mapping, settlement windows, duplicate protection, exception queue and ownership.","An API response is not settlement proof. Trace state and reconcile independent records before retrying."],t.l)
B.My=new A.b4(B.aG,["Source completeness: eligible transactions = successfully processed + explicitly rejected/held items after documented exclusions. Reconcile count and value.","Write a timeout-handling flow including ID, status inquiry, idempotency, bounded retry, exception route and audit log.","Design ERP-to-provider integration controls for API contract, access, retries, monitoring, reconciliation and incidents.","Design for timeouts and retries; use idempotency to avoid duplicate effects and reconcile transaction outcomes."],t.l)
B.MC=new A.b4(B.aG,["A simple risk-priority score may be likelihood \xd7 impact, but treat it as a ranking aid unless supported by validated quantitative evidence.","Create a bank-detail-change checklist covering trusted-channel verification, maker-checker, access, evidence and escalation.","Run a tabletop exercise for payment redirection: detection, containment, evidence, stakeholders, recovery and lessons learned.","Independently verify sensitive changes, restrict access, preserve evidence and escalate suspicious activity."],t.l)
B.KN=s([B.MI,B.My,B.MC],t.SN)
B.MA=new A.b4(B.aG,["Improvement % = (baseline \u2212 new result) \xf7 baseline \xd7 100% for lower-is-better measures, where baseline is non-zero.","Map a blocked-invoice process, identify five handoffs and three possible root causes, and specify evidence needed to validate them.","Create a problem statement, current-state map, root-cause summary and prioritised improvement backlog.","Measure first, map real work and validate root causes before selecting a solution."],t.l)
B.MD=new A.b4(B.aG,["Story format: As a [role], I want [capability], so that [business value]. Criteria must be specific, observable and testable.","Write a user story and five pass/fail criteria for reducing blocked invoices, including reconciliation, exception visibility and access control.","Prepare a backlog item with problem, story, criteria, dependencies, risks, tests and Definition of Done.","A story explains who needs what and why; acceptance criteria prove the outcome; Definition of Done protects quality."],t.l)
